+# Milestone 1.1 — Named-file counting
+
+## Boundary and delivered result
+
+T-004 reviews the complete named-file counting capability under accepted SPEC R-001 through R-007 and milestone 1.1 PLAN exits, with relevant R-012 checks. Reviewed source is `373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b` on `phase/1-named-file-utility`, containing T-001 `9dc8075dd1b96d3a2744717a9d6d98a3024acbec`, T-002 `f28f6e415b3e0c13353a61e82354c47b0d2cabb2` and T-003 `373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b`. Each result/evidence/initial task checkbox is owned by its separate single-ID task commit. All three commits were published and read back before subsequent task work; their uniquely marked maintained issues #2, #3 and #4 are closed/completed. T-004 is uniquely associated with issue #5 and native milestone #1.
+
+Delivered immutable validated TextStats, silent whole-input text and named-file APIs, complete strict UTF-8 acquisition with owned-handle cleanup, exact named-file module output, BOM option, option termination and help. Unit/integration suites are independently discovered and required to be nonempty. The phase remains incomplete: no merge into main, release, next milestone or later phase is authorized by this milestone checkpoint.
+
+## Implementation code review
+
+Read-only review inspected all five product modules, the product runner, unit and integration tests, source docstrings and current README/orientation against accepted SPEC/PLAN/design/layout. Code review is distinct from the test runs below.
+
+| Concern | Inspection result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Value/API contract | Frozen slotted value validates nonnegative integers and excludes bool; fields have value equality. Direct exports/signatures and keyword-only whole-input policy are preserved; imports/calls have no output effects. |
+| Semantics/extension seams | Shared traversal counts only CRLF/CR/LF and preserves terminators. Once-only complete-input BOM normalization precedes normalized counting; Unicode word splitting is independent. Internal seams support future source-independent selection without adding range behavior. |
+| Acquisition/lifetime | Binary context-managed complete read avoids newline translation, strict UTF-8 decode occurs before counting, and owned handles close on read/decode/success paths. Applicable exceptions propagate without partial result or input writes. No fallback decoding or CLI dependency. |
+| CLI/data flow | Argparse validates one named input and handles help before acquisition. BOM policy and `--` termination flow into count_file; only a completed result is printed in exact format. Literal `-` remains a filename. Minimal module entry returns controller status. |
+| Collection and test quality | Independent explicit unit/integration roots exclude workflow fixtures. Actual counts are reported and either zero blocks success; test failure propagates. Real subprocess and temporary-file tests complement narrow portable failure streams; independent literal expected counts anchor core/CLI semantics. |
+| Documentation/scope | Module/function docs and root navigation accurately describe delivered success/API capabilities and planned failure/docs/distribution scope. No governing requirement was changed, no extra API/JSON/stdin/range was added. |
+
+Findings/Blockers: None for milestone 1.1. No production repair was needed during T-004. Complete R-008 CLI failure diagnostics remain a separately planned milestone 1.2 obligation; their absence is not deferred milestone 1.1 defect acceptance. Standalone API documentation, source distribution and later formats/input sources likewise retain their accepted future tasks.
+
+## Checks and actual outcomes
+
+On Python 3.12.14, commands ran from the product repository root at the reviewed source:
+
+| Check | Observed outcome and coverage |
+| --- | --- |
+| `python tools/check_tests.py` | Status 0; 21 unit and 12 integration tests passed, zero skips/warnings. Core whole-input matrix/BOM/Unicode/value invariants, real-file equivalence/preservation/API silence, strict exceptions/owned cleanup, CLI success/help/option order/dash names and runner collection/failure contracts. |
+| Real UTF-8 mixed-terminator demonstration | Temporary file contained leading BOM plus `α\r\n猫\rβ γ\n`. Both API and `python -m textstats INPUT` / `python -m textstats --keep-bom INPUT` returned three lines/four words; process status 0, stdout exactly `lines=3 words=4\n`, stderr empty, original bytes unchanged. |
+| BOM-only demonstration | Default module invocation emitted exactly `lines=0 words=0\n`; `--keep-bom` emitted `lines=1 words=1\n`; both status 0 with empty stderr. This makes the retaining policy visible. |
+| Source, task persistence and document inspection | Reviewed exact source and separate task closing diffs; all public/module docstrings reflect delivered contracts. Current local navigation and heading/list spacing were inspected; staged diff whitespace is checked before the report commit. Protected resources are outside the product delta. |
+
+Prior T-002/T-003 behavioral RED evidence and development GREEN checks are retained in TASKS. This review reused those contract cases and performed the actual complete runner and useful demonstration on the published integrated capability. No fabricated prior RED or test-first exception is claimed.
+
+## Exit assessment and limits
+
+All milestone 1.1 exits are verified: complete public whole-input API, sample matrix, immutability/silence, strict named-file decoding/cleanup/exceptions, real CLI named-file/BOM/help/dash-filename success, input preservation, meaningful nonempty suites and useful API/module demonstration. Verification establishes this runtime and phase-branch capability; it does not establish every supported Python version/platform, platform-specific permission enforcement, complete CLI failure robustness, public guide/source-distribution acceptance or full phase/project completion. Portable controlled PermissionError/read streams complement actual temporary-file decode/equivalence tests.
+
+The milestone report and initial T-004 checkbox close together in one task commit. Eligible milestone 1.1 parent completion accompanies this final task on verified local exits; hosted issue #5 and milestone #1 closure/readback follow its commit/push. Those subsequent states must be reported from actual provider observations, not assumed here. Phase 1 and all unselected tasks remain unchecked.
+
+## TODO
+
+None.
+
+## Stopping point
+
+Stop after publishing/readback of T-004 and its verified issue/milestone reconciliation. Retain `phase/1-named-file-utility`; do not merge the incomplete phase, start T-005, activate phase 2, implement range or publish a release.
